#
# Strategy: directory structure (`<page>/index.html`) + this _redirects file.
# - <page>/ (with trailing slash) is served directly by Pages as the
#   directory's index.html — 200 OK, 0 redirects, served cleanly.
# - <page>.html is 308'd to <page>/ for back-compat with old external
#   links / old Google index / any hard-coded .html URLs.
#
# We do NOT add rules for the no-extension no-slash form (e.g. /about).
# Pages' default 308 behavior for those is acceptable as a single back-compat
# hop. The internal site never links to that form.
#
# Why so few rules: more rules = more chances of self-redirects and
# conflict with Pages' own normalization (which strips trailing slashes
# before matching rules). Keep this minimal.
# === Blog 01-50 -> semantic-slug migration (auto-generated) ===
# When: 2026-07-23 (rename-blog-dirs.py).
# Purpose: external links / social shares pointing at the old numeric
